// P3.4 / PS8: the course's Reducer Coupling exercise (intro-to-part-studios.md PS8, drawings
// ex2-step2, ex2-step4, ex2-step6, screenshots ex2-step1..10), step by step, in inches.
// 01 (ex2-step1) Workspace units: Length units Inch, Mass units Pound (P3.5: the course works in
//    inches and pounds); the document and its Part Studio renamed
//    "Reducer Coupling", the Assembly tab deleted (02).
// 03 (ex2-step2) Sketch 1 on Right: Ø6 and the Ø2 bore on the origin, a Ø4.75 construction
//    bolt circle with 4 × Ø0.625 holes at the quadrants (Equal, Horizontal and Vertical with the
//    origin). The planes are hidden (P).
// 04 (ex2-step3) Extrude 1, Solid / New, Blind 0.62 in towards +X, the whole sketch ("Sketch
//    1": the bore and the holes left out).
// 05 (ex2-step4) Sketch 2 on Front: Use of the bore's edge on the flange's face (a vertical
//    line), a horizontal construction centreline from the origin, the four-sided profile from
//    the top of the projected line (its slanted sides Parallel, its ends vertical), and the
//    diametral dimensions Ø2.625 and Ø3.75 to the centreline (the point, the centreline, the
//    label placed across it) and the 4.625 axial length.
// 06 (ex2-step5) Revolve 1 (Shift+W): Solid, Add (picked by itself: it touches the flange),
//    "Face of Sketch 2", Revolve axis "Edge of Sketch 2" (the centreline), Full, Merge with all.
// 07 (ex2-step6) Sketch 3 on the revolve's end face: Use of its inner edge (Ø3.125), Ø7.5, a Ø6
//    construction bolt circle and 4 × Ø0.75 holes at the quadrants.
// 08 (ex2-step7) Extrude 2, Add, Blind 0.75 in, the whole of Sketch 3, Merge with all, with the
//    drag arrow on the added flange.
// 09 (ex2-step8) the part's context menu in the Parts list; Rename → "Reducer Coupling" (10).
// 11 (ex2-step10) the part selected, Mass and section properties: Volume 53.932 in³, Surface
//    area 248.367 in² (the course's self-check; both asserted in
//    `cadrs_core/tests/revolve.rs`), the inertia heading in in² lb.
